- Report only what the inputs actually show. If a project's month contains nothing that reaches outside it, say so in one line — never invent a version, an API change or a migration.
- The rollup must NOT paste raw issue/MR bodies verbatim; if a description is needed, summarize it in one short sentence and reference the URL.
- Output Markdown only. No preamble. Start with a summary paragraph aimed at a reader outside these projects: what changed this month and what, if anything, they have to do about it.
- Do not write a title of your own: no line starting with "# ". The document already carries its title, and a second one in the body is a duplicate. Section headings ("## ...") are fine and make the changes easier to find.

